Key advanced topic areas in Angular 21
the main areas are:(https://dev.to/koolkamalkishor/angular-advanced-qa-a-comprehensive-guide-pbg)
Change detection & performance 

Default vs OnPush

trackBy in *ngFor

Lazy loading modules/routes

Tree shaking, bundle optimization, virtual scroll.(https://frontendmasters.com/courses/advanced-angular/)

Signals & state management

Angular Signals API (signal vs observable)

local component state with signals

app‑wide state with SignalStore, NgRx, and hybrid patterns.(https://www.linkedin.com/posts/kundan-k-534676bb_angular-frontend-webdevelopment-share-7429468683011420161--6Hu/)

Dependency injection & application architecture

DI hierarchy, providers in modules vs components

standalone components & modern bootstrapping

feature, shared, and core modules (for mixed setups).(https://dev.to/koolkamalkishor/angular-advanced-qa-a-comprehensive-guide-pbg)

Advanced RxJS usage

switchMap vs mergeMap vs concatMap vs exhaustMap

canceling HTTP requests, avoiding memory leaks

Subject, BehaviorSubject, ReplaySubject and composition patterns.

Routing, guards, and security

complex routing, lazy routes, route guards

role‑based access control (RBAC)

HttpInterceptors for auth, logging, and error handling.

Testing and enterprise concerns

harnesses and DOM‑interaction tests

SSR (Angular Universal) vs CSR

micro‑frontend architecture and modularization.

Strong resources to go deep
1) Advanced Angular courses
Frontend Masters – Advanced Angular: Performance & Enterprise State

URL: [Advanced Angular: Performance & Enterprise State]

Focus: cutting‑edge optimization, Signals with SignalStore, NgRx at scale, and serious testing strategies.

Very good if you want senior‑level performance and state‑architecture competence for Angular 21.

Coursera – Advanced Angular Topics

URL: [Advanced Angular Topics]

Covers advanced routing, forms, directives, and more structured topics suitable as a step up from beginner courses.

CodeSignal Learn – Advanced Angular Concepts

URL: [Advanced Angular Concepts]

Focus: deeper forms, directives, i18n, and basic state‑management techniques—nice for hands‑on exercises.

2) Angular 21 full-course outlines (to see the full landscape)
Angular 21 complete course content (Ashok IT)

PDF outline: [Angular 21 – Complete Course Content]

Shows a modern curriculum from basics to advanced, including:

Signals and state patterns (Module 19)

Performance optimization (Module 20)

Authentication, interceptors, and architecture modules.

Useful as a checklist of what “advanced Angular 21” should cover.

Jegan’s Angular 21 3‑day outline

PDF: [Angular 21 outline]

Short, intensive outline that touches performance, forms, routing, DI, and HTTP—good to see what a fast-track advanced course includes.

